{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-recording-tree-003-01", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs", "line": 3145, "method": "PopulateLoopSync_NonDebrisGetsMinusOne", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingStore.Optimization.cs:582; write 0 instead of -1 in the non-debris early-out -> red", "what_it_asserts": "PopulateLoopSyncParentIndices leaves LoopSyncParentIdx at -1 for a non-debris recording.", "why_weak": "The fixture list holds only the non-debris recording itself, so no candidate can ever be found; removing the debris/TreeId early-out at RecordingStore.Optimization.cs:580 leaves the cell green because Recording.LoopSyncParentIdx defaults to -1. The cell fails only on a wrong non--1 write.", "proposed_action": "Add a second non-debris recording in the same tree whose UT range covers the first recording's StartUT and assert both stay -1, so the cell pins the debris-only guard instead of the field default.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-recording-tree-003-02", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs", "line": 3164, "method": "PopulateLoopSync_DebrisWithoutMatchingParent_GetsMinusOne", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingStore.Optimization.cs:588; initialize int parentIdx = 0 -> red", "what_it_asserts": "A debris recording with no non-debris recording covering its StartUT keeps LoopSyncParentIdx at -1.", "why_weak": "The list contains only the debris, so no candidate exists and the same-tree/vessel/UT-range conjuncts at RecordingStore.Optimization.cs:593-596 are never exercised; deleting them leaves the cell green. The named no-match contract is not distinguished from the default -1.", "proposed_action": "Add a same-tree non-debris recording whose UT range does not cover the debris StartUT (keep a covering one as positive control), so dropping the range check reds.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-recording-tree-003-03", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs", "line": 3184, "method": "PopulateLoopSync_DebrisWithoutTreeId_GetsMinusOne", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingStore.Optimization.cs:582; write 0 instead of -1 in the early-out -> red", "what_it_asserts": "A debris recording with TreeId=null keeps LoopSyncParentIdx at -1.", "why_weak": "The fixture has no other recording, so removing the TreeId conjunct from the early-out at RecordingStore.Optimization.cs:580 still yields -1 and stays green; only a wrong non--1 write fails it.", "proposed_action": "Pair the null-TreeId debris with a non-debris recording that carries a tree id and covers its StartUT; dropping the TreeId guard then links the pair and reds.", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
{"kind": "finding", "id": "F-recording-tree-003-04", "file": "Source/Parsek.Tests/RecordingOptimizerTests.cs", "line": 3710, "method": "TrimBoringTail_PreservesBufferSeconds", "category": "T3", "severity": "Medium", "confidence": "high", "falsifiability": "falsifiability: Source/Parsek/RecordingOptimizer.TailTrim.cs:671; use 2.0 * bufferSeconds -> EndUT 17070 -> red", "what_it_asserts": "After TrimBoringTail the recording's EndUT lies within [lastInterestingUT, lastInterestingUT+buffer] (17050..17060).", "why_weak": "Both bounds hold for a zero buffer too: with DefaultTailBufferSeconds=0 the trim keeps the point at UT 17050 and EndUT=17050 passes; the cell pins no-more-than-buffer, not the 10 s buffer, so a buffer regression ships green.", "proposed_action": "Assert the exact trimmed end (Assert.Equal(17060, rec.EndUT)) or make the lower bound strict (Assert.True(rec.EndUT > 17050)).", "effort": "S", "july_ref": "none"}
